    <node id="Quercetin">
      <data key="d0">Quercetin</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Quercetin is a flavonoid found in many fruits and vegetables, known for its antioxidant properties and potential anti-cancer effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid that can act as a regulator of drug resistance proteins and is derived from various fruits and vegetables.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid that can regulate drug resistance proteins and has been noted for its potential health benefits, including anti-inflammatory effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid that can regulate histone proteins and is noted for its potential to influence drug resistance mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid that supports breast cancer treatment by activating receptors that make cancer cells more responsive to treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid with antioxidant properties that may help in regulating cancer-related pathways in breast cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid with antioxidant properties that may help reduce inflammation and support immune function.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid with antioxidant properties that may play a role in cancer treatment and prevention.&lt;SEP&gt;Quercetin is a flavonoid with antioxidant properties, often studied for its potential health benefits including anti-cancer effects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0633d0c9fbeab3f25914885985ace04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c8a13a1d7994bb3d188bcbdc68feefa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea5b318e2a8248e37e47eace395c05b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c06ae3e33dd062c6f8cbc3263674c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2405fce9bf1e9596eff6dd81273a458&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0049dde5f6453f5037ca54e07e32cce4</data>
