    </node>
    <node id="Resveratrol">
      <data key="d0">Resveratrol</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Resveratrol is a compound found in Muscadine grapes that exhibits phytoestrogen properties and its safety varies by menopausal status.&lt;SEP&gt;Resveratrol is a phytoestrogen that blocks estrogen DNA adducts responsible for breast cancer, though its safety in post-menopausal ER+ women is still under research.&lt;SEP&gt;Resveratrol is a phytoestrogen that blocks estrogen DNA adducts, which are linked to breast cancer, and binds to estrogen receptors.&lt;SEP&gt;Resveratrol is a natural compound found in grapes and berries, known for its antioxidant properties and potential health benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;Resveratrol is a natural compound found in grapes and berries, known for its antioxidant properties and potential health benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f0633d0c9fbeab3f25914885985ace04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b81d9e841623e400ca410d21b5046cb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c8a13a1d7994bb3d188bcbdc68feefa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0049dde5f6453f5037ca54e07e32cce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17fa5148a048f188a17fb9ca3e127d27</data>
