    <node id="Curcumin">
      <data key="d0">Curcumin</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Curcumin is a bioactive compound found in turmeric, known for its anti-inflammatory and anti-cancer properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a compound found in turmeric that has anti-inflammatory properties and can inhibit prostaglandin production, impacting drug resistance mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a compound found in turmeric that has potential effects on histone proteins and may help mitigate drug resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a compound found in turmeric, known for its anti-inflammatory and antioxidant effects, often used in cancer treatment protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a natural compound with anti-inflammatory properties, suggested for various health benefits including bone health.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a phytochemical that can modulate histone protein acylation and has potential effects on drug resistance mechanisms in cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a compound found in turmeric that has anti-inflammatory properties and is explored for its potential benefits in cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is the active compound in turmeric, known for its anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a phytochemical with anti-inflammatory and anti-cancer properties, often studied for its role in cancer prevention.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a natural compound found in turmeric, known for its anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Curcumin is a bioactive compound found in turmeric, recognized for its anti-inflammatory and anti-cancer properties.</data>
